{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED on exact clean pushed head 2eaf52bfe73d5b841f8a7922209b326f5f2e6667. Independent gates passed: go test ./internal/kernel -count=1 in 103.295s, go test -race ./internal/kernel in 114.131s, go vet ./internal/kernel, clean tree, exact origin head, and git diff --check. Do not merge this head.\n\nArchitecture: the affected layers are Ordinary Git storage and the Kernel, specifically the compact checkpoint cache and serialized checkpoint boundary. The kernel/application separation is preserved, but the layer contract changes: checkpointLimitWriter is also used by marshalCompactCheckpoint, so the universal half-budget rule lowers the largest writable serialized checkpoint from the documented 256 MiB to about 128 MiB. docs/reference/limits.md still promises a 256 MiB serialized checkpoint blob, and request d6e869e9 did not authorize reducing what can be published. Preserve the 256 MiB marshal ceiling and scope cache growth-copy headroom to cache chunk construction, or update the architecture and limits contract under separately authorized scope.\n\nSecurity: the trust boundary receives untrusted, potentially incompressible event payloads and attachments. The exact head fixes the early in-hand credit and charges retained clone capacity, but three peak-bound defects remain. First, append preflights source lengths and then allocates checkpointMaterial with bytes.Clone; the head own capacity test proves a clone can retain more than source length. The post-clone check therefore rejects only after the allocation has already exceeded the remaining allowance. Refuse against a conservative clone bound before allocation or clone into explicitly bounded storage. Second, c.chunks grows with every compressed chunk, but chunkBytes counts only output.Cap and never the backing array of the [][]byte slice; charge and preflight that growing metadata. Third, appendBorrowedChunk and flushTail call c.fail before compressed.Close on write failure. fail clears the reserve, so Close may flush and grow the local output against a newly enlarged budget while dropped chunks, tail storage, and the in-hand material remain live until collection. Keep reservations through compressor cleanup or abandon the failed compressor without flushing, then release storage. Add mutation-sensitive witnesses for these paths.\n\nSimplification: one writer policy currently conflates two different guarantees: bounded cache construction and the final 256 MiB serialized artifact. Split the cache-specific growth-headroom policy from the marshal output limit. That both preserves the existing contract and removes the misleading universal half-budget behavior. Remove or correct the false claim that the length preflight makes the clone transient always fit. Keep the useful in-hand timing and cloned-capacity tests; add a test pinning successful serialization above half the limit and tests covering chunk-slice accounting and overflow cleanup.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a867add6c74724b13742861d3caf1717422ebe2e","head":"2eaf52bfe73d5b841f8a7922209b326f5f2e6667","verdict":"changes-requested"}}